14:55:22   5. WHERE CONDITIONS MOVE THE ODDS - a preview of the conditional tables (Phase C)
14:55:22      LIFT = (realised - baseline) in the group, minus the same miss over ALL rows of that
14:55:22      year - so a drift that lifts every group at once (a bull year, cheaper trades) is
14:55:22      taken out and only what the condition adds is left. Percentage points. Listed only
14:55:22      when the lift has the SAME sign in all three years AND its 90% interval excludes 0.
14:55:22      A lift is a candidate, not a forecast: Phase C has to turn it into one and beat the
14:55:22      baseline out of sample, with a penalty for how many candidates were looked at.
14:55:22      38 of 288 condition groups met both tests. By chance alone about 22 would
14:55:22      (90% range 14-29); more than that suggests some structure is real, but not WHICH rows.
